  - differential privacy
  - behavioral identity
  - cybersecurity
  - insider threat
abstract: >
  The Sentinel Ego is a federated adversarial deception framework that combines
  Persistent Behavioral Identity (PBI) generation, Adversarial Interaction
  Fingerprinting (AIF), Federated Adversarial Learning (FAL) with differential
  privacy, Collective Deception Evolution (CDE), and Mirror Defense into a unified
  five-phase system for enterprise intrusion detection and behavioral deception.
  Evaluated on real Enron email data and three network intrusion benchmarks
  (NSL-KDD, KDDCup99-SF, NetIntrusion), the system achieves F1=0.9994 with a
  formal (1.2802, 1e-5)-DP guarantee under Rényi DP accounting.
